{"id": "EUVD-2026-101719", "enisaUuid": "4375c5de-088c-3133-bb79-4ff90278ee5d", "description": "FreeRDP from 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains an infinite loop vulnerability in http_response_recv() that allows malicious gateways to exhaust client CPU via crafted Content-Type headers. Attackers controlling a gateway can return a nonzero Content-Length with a semicolon-containing unrecognized Content-Type, pinning a client thread at full CPU indefinitely.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T02:17:21", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-h7fx-22wv-4cg8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-infinite-loop-dos-via-gateway-content-type"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2h9m-vq46-2fq9", "CVE-2026-110836"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "823b091b-1ca0-35cd-a699-0b670e53a49e", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d2fbfd4a-6aec-35fd-96c7-5c8cb2d80c1e", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}